  "solution": "The correct answer is: **2) DNS translates domain names into IP addresses to allow browsers to locate web servers.**\n\n**__Explanation:__**\n\nDNS acts as the \"phonebook of the internet,\" converting human-readable domain names (like www.example.com) into numeric IP addresses that computers use to route communications. It does not handle packet routing (that’s the job of routers and the IP protocol), nor is its primary role encryption (security is managed by protocols like TLS/SSL). Reverse DNS (IP to domain name) exists, but the essential function of DNS is domain name → IP address translation.\n\n \n\n<path d=\"M6.14923 4.02032C7.11191 4.02032 7.87977 4.02017 8.49591 4.07599C9.12122 4.1327 9.65786 4.25188 10.1414 4.53107C10.7201 4.8653 11.2008 5.34591 11.535 5.92462C11.8142 6.40818 11.9333 6.94482 11.9901 7.57013C12.0459 8.18625 12.0457 8.9542 12.0457 9.91681C12.0457 10.8795 12.0459 11.6474 11.9901 12.2635C11.9333 12.8888 11.8142 13.4254 11.535 13.909C11.2008 14.4877 10.7201 14.9683 10.1414 15.3026C9.65786 15.5817 9.12122 15.7009 8.49591 15.7576C7.87977 15.8134 7.1119 15.8133 6.14923 15.8133C5.18661 15.8133 4.41868 15.8134 3.80255 15.7576C3.17724 15.7009 2.6406 15.5817 2.15704 15.3026C1.57834 14.9684 1.09772 14.4877 0.763489 13.909C0.484305 13.4254 0.365123 12.8888 0.308411 12.2635C0.252587 11.6474 0.252747 10.8795 0.252747 9.91681C0.252747 8.95419 0.252603 8.18625 0.308411 7.57013C0.365123 6.94482 0.484305 6.40818 0.763489 5.92462C1.09771 5.3459 1.57833 4.86529 2.15704 4.53107C2.6406 4.25188 3.17724 4.1327 3.80255 4.07599C4.41868 4.02018 5.1866 4.02032 6.14923 4.02032ZM6.14923 5.37775C5.16175 5.37775 4.46628 5.37761 3.9256 5.42657C3.39428 5.47473 3.07853 5.56574 2.83575 5.70587C2.46313 5.92106 2.15348 6.23071 1.93829 6.60333C1.79817 6.84611 1.70715 7.16185 1.659 7.69318C1.61004 8.23385 1.61017 8.92934 1.61017 9.91681C1.61017 10.9043 1.61002 11.5998 1.659 12.1404C1.70715 12.6717 1.79817 12.9875 1.93829 13.2303C2.15349 13.6029 2.46315 13.9126 2.835